import Mathlib.LinearAlgebra.Dimension.OrzechProperty

/-!
# The quadratic part of a hypersurface at a node

Let `P` be a local `K`-algebra with coordinates `x : ι → P` generating its maximal ideal `𝔪`,
whose differentials `dxᵢ` form a basis of `Ω[P⁄K]`: for instance the local ring at a closed point
of a smooth variety, with coordinates centred there. Let `f ∈ 𝔪`, so that `A = P ⧸ (f)` is the
local ring at a point of the hypersurface `f = 0`. With `n = |ι|`, the `(n - 1)`-st Fitting
ideal of `Ω[A⁄K]` is generated by the partial derivatives `∂f/∂xᵢ`
(`TauCeti.fittingIdeal_kaehlerDifferential_quotient_span_singleton`). When `P` is the local ring
at a closed point of a smooth `n`-dimensional variety over a field `K` and `f ≠ 0`, so that `A`
is the local ring of a hypersurface of dimension `n - 1`, this Fitting ideal cuts out the
singular locus of `A`; the results below are stated for the Fitting ideal itself.

The scheme-theoretic criterion for a node asks that this singular locus be unramified over `K`
and pass through the closed point. This file shows that it forces the quadratic part of `f` to
be nondegenerate: `f ∈ 𝔪²`, and the Hessian determinant `det (∂²f/∂xᵢ∂xⱼ)` is a unit, that is,
the polar form of the quadratic part of `f` is nondegenerate. More precisely, the closed
subscheme cut out by the Fitting ideal is the reduced closed point exactly when these two
conditions hold.
For a plane curve, `n = 2`, and writing `f = a s² + b s t + c t²` with `a, b, c ∈ P`, the
second condition says that the discriminant `b² - 4ac` is a unit
(`TauCeti.isUnit_det_hessian_iff_isUnit_discrim`). Geometrically, the quadratic part of `f` then
cuts out two distinct lines in the tangent plane, possibly conjugate over a separable quadratic
extension of the residue field; they are the tangent directions of the two branches through the
node, which this file does not construct.

The same holds over an arbitrary base, at a point that need not be closed. Let `W` be an
`R`-algebra whose differentials have a basis indexed by `ι`, with dual partial derivatives `∂ᵢ`;
for instance a smooth relative surface over `R` on which `Ω[W⁄R]` is free, containing a relative
plane curve `f = 0`. If the Fitting-ideal locus of `W ⧸ (f)` is unramified over `R`, then at
every prime `𝔭` of `W` lying in it, `f` is critical (`∂ᵢ f ∈ 𝔭`) and its Hessian determinant is
not in `𝔭`. When moreover `W` is smooth over `R` and the basis is indexed by `Fin 2`, this is the
input that `Module.Basis.exists_etale_eq_algebraMap_add_quadratic` needs to put `f`, étale
locally around `𝔭`, in the form `h + a s² + b s t + c t²`. The local statement above is the
special case where `W = P` is a local `K`-algebra and `𝔭 = 𝔪`.

## Main results

* `TauCeti.comap_fittingIdeal_kaehlerDifferential_eq_maximalIdeal_iff`: the closed subscheme of
  `f = 0` cut out by the `(n - 1)`-st Fitting ideal of its differentials is the reduced closed
  point exactly when `f ∈ 𝔪²` and the Hessian determinant of `f` is a unit.
* `Module.Basis.forall_mem_and_det_hessian_notMem_of_formallyUnramified`: over any base `R`, if
  the Fitting-ideal locus of `W ⧸ (f)` is unramified, then at every prime `𝔭` in it the partial
  derivatives of `f` lie in `𝔭` and its Hessian determinant does not.
* `TauCeti.mem_maximalIdeal_sq_and_isUnit_det_hessian_of_formallyUnramified`: if this closed
  subscheme of `P ⧸ (f)` is unramified and contains the closed point, then `f ∈ 𝔪²` and the
  Hessian determinant of `f` is a unit.

## References

* [Stacks Project, Section 53.19, Tag 0C46](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C46): nodes of
  curves, defined by a nondegenerate quadratic form in two variables.
* [Stacks Project, Lemma 53.20.1, Tag 0C58](https://stacks.math.columbia.edu/tag/0C58): the
  singular-locus criterion for families of nodal curves.
-/

public section

noncomputable section

open IsLocalRing KaehlerDifferential

namespace TauCeti

section Relative

open TensorProduct

variable {A W : Type*} [CommRing A] [CommRing W] [Algebra A W] {ι : Type*} [Fintype ι]
  [DecidableEq ι] [Nonempty ι]

/-- **A node of a hypersurface over any base has nondegenerate quadratic part.** Let `b` be a basis
of `Ω[W⁄A]` indexed by `ι`, with dual partial derivatives `∂ᵢ`, and let `f ∈ W`. Suppose that the
closed subscheme of `W ⧸ (f)` cut out by the `(|ι| - 1)`-st Fitting ideal of its differentials
(the singular locus, when `W` is smooth over `A` of relative dimension `|ι|` and `W ⧸ (f)` is flat
over `A` of relative dimension `|ι| - 1`) is unramified over `A`, and let `P` be a prime of `W`
whose image lies in it. Then `f` is critical at `P`, that is `∂ᵢ f ∈ P` for all `i`, and its
Hessian determinant `det (∂ᵢ ∂ⱼ f)` does not lie in `P`. The base `A` is arbitrary, and `P`
need not be maximal. -/
theorem _root_.Module.Basis.forall_mem_and_det_hessian_notMem_of_formallyUnramified
    (b : Module.Basis ι W Ω[W⁄A]) (f : W)
    [Module.Finite (W ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) Ω[(W ⧸ Ideal.span {f})⁄A]]
    [Algebra.FormallyUnramified A ((W ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) ⧸
      fittingIdeal (W ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) Ω[(W ⧸ Ideal.span {f})⁄A] (Fintype.card ι - 1))]
    (P : Ideal W) [P.IsPrime]
    (hP : (fittingIdeal (W ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) Ω[(W ⧸ Ideal.span {f})⁄A]
      (Fintype.card ι - 1)).comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk _) ≤ P) :
    (∀ i, (b.coord i).compDer (D A W) f ∈ P) ∧
      (hessian (fun i ↦ (b.coord i).compDer (D A W)) f).det ∉ P := by
  set d : ι → Derivation A W W := fun i ↦ (b.coord i).compDer (D A W)
  set I := fittingIdeal (W ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) Ω[(W ⧸ Ideal.span {f})⁄A] (Fintype.card ι - 1)
  -- The singular locus is the quotient of `W` by the Jacobian ideal `(f, ∂ᵢ f)`, since the
  -- Fitting ideal is generated by the `∂ᵢ f`.
  set s : Set W := insert f (Set.range fun i ↦ d i f)
  have hs : I.comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk _) = Ideal.span s := by
    simpa [s, d] using comap_fittingIdeal_kaehlerDifferential_quotient_span_singleton f b
  let g : W →ₐ[A] (W ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) ⧸ I :=
    (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A I).comp (Ideal.Quotient.mkₐ A (Ideal.span {f}))
  have hg : Function.Surjective g :=
    Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective.comp Ideal.Quotient.mk_surjective
  have hker : RingHom.ker g = Ideal.span s := by
    rw [← hs]
    ext p
    simp [g, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem]
  have : Algebra.FormallyUnramified A (W ⧸ Ideal.span s) :=
    .of_equiv ((Ideal.quotientKerAlgEquivOfSurjective hg).symm.trans
      (Ideal.quotientEquivAlgOfEq A hker))
  have hsP : Ideal.span s ≤ P := hs ▸ hP
  have hd (i : ι) : d i f ∈ P := hsP (Ideal.subset_span (Set.mem_insert_of_mem _ ⟨i, rfl⟩))
  refine ⟨hd, fun hdet ↦ ?_⟩
  -- As the singular locus is unramified, the `1 ⊗ dg` for `g ∈ s` span `κ(P) ⊗[W] Ω[W⁄A]`.
  -- Among them `1 ⊗ df` vanishes, as its coordinates are the `∂ᵢ f ∈ P`.
  set κ := P.ResidueField
  have hspan := span_one_tmul_D_eq_top_of_formallyUnramified (K := A) s κ fun g hg ↦
    Ideal.algebraMap_residueField_eq_zero.2 (hsP (Ideal.subset_span hg))
  let bκ := Algebra.TensorProduct.basis κ b
  have hf : (1 : κ) ⊗ₜ[W] D A W f = 0 := by
    refine bκ.repr.injective (Finsupp.ext fun i ↦ ?_)
    simp only [bκ, Algebra.TensorProduct.basis_repr_tmul, map_zero, Finsupp.coe_zero,
      Pi.zero_apply, Finsupp.mapRange_apply, one_smul]
    exact Ideal.algebraMap_residueField_eq_zero.2 (by simpa [d] using hd i)
  -- So the `|ι|` elements `1 ⊗ d(∂ⱼ f)` span, hence form a basis; their determinant is the
  -- Hessian determinant modulo `P`.
  set v : ι → κ ⊗[W] Ω[W⁄A] := fun j ↦ (1 : κ) ⊗ₜ D A W (d j f)
  have hv : Submodule.span κ (Set.range v) = ⊤ := by
    rw [← hspan, Set.image_insert_eq, hf, Submodule.span_insert_zero, ← Set.range_comp]
    simp [v, Function.comp_def]
  have hli : LinearIndependent κ v := linearIndependent_of_top_le_span_of_card_eq_finrank hv.ge
    (by rw [Module.finrank_eq_card_basis bκ])
  have hunit := bκ.is_basis_iff_det.1 ⟨hli, hv⟩
  have hdetv : bκ.det v = algebraMap W κ (hessian d f).det := by
    rw [Module.Basis.det_apply, RingHom.map_det]
    congr 1
    ext i j
    simp [bκ, v, Module.Basis.toMatrix_apply, Algebra.TensorProduct.basis_repr_tmul, hessian_apply,
      d]
  rw [hdetv, Ideal.algebraMap_residueField_eq_zero.2 hdet] at hunit
  exact not_isUnit_zero hunit

end Relative

variable {K P ι : Type*} [CommRing P] [IsLocalRing P] [Fintype ι] [DecidableEq ι] [Nonempty ι]
  {x : ι → P} {f : P}

/-- **The Fitting ideal of a hypersurface with nondegenerate Hessian.** If the differentials
`dxᵢ` of coordinates generating `𝔪` form a basis of `Ω[P⁄K]`, and `f ∈ 𝔪`, then the closed
subscheme of `P ⧸ (f)` cut out by the `(|ι| - 1)`-st Fitting ideal of its differentials (the
singular locus, in the smooth setting of the module docstring) is the reduced closed point exactly
when `f ∈ 𝔪²` and the Hessian determinant of `f` is a unit. -/
theorem comap_fittingIdeal_kaehlerDifferential_eq_maximalIdeal_iff [CommRing K] [Algebra K P]
    [Module.Finite (P ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) Ω[(P ⧸ Ideal.span {f})⁄K]]
    (b : Module.Basis ι P Ω[P⁄K]) (hx : maximalIdeal P = Ideal.span (Set.range x))
    (hb : ∀ i, b i = D K P (x i)) (hf : f ∈ maximalIdeal P) :
    (fittingIdeal (P ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) Ω[(P ⧸ Ideal.span {f})⁄K] (Fintype.card ι - 1)).comap
        (Ideal.Quotient.mk _) = maximalIdeal P ↔
      f ∈ maximalIdeal P ^ 2 ∧ IsUnit (hessian (fun i ↦ (b.coord i).compDer (D K P)) f).det := by
  have hD (i j : ι) : (b.coord i).compDer (D K P) (x j) = if i = j then 1 else 0 := by
    simp [← hb, Finsupp.single_apply, eq_comm]
  rw [← span_range_apply_sup_span_singleton_eq_maximalIdeal_iff hx hD hf,
    comap_fittingIdeal_kaehlerDifferential_quotient_span_singleton f b, Ideal.span_insert,
    sup_comm]
  simp

/-- **The quadratic part of `f` at a node is nondegenerate.** Let the differentials `dxᵢ` of
coordinates generating `𝔪` form a basis of `Ω[P⁄K]`. If the closed subscheme of `P ⧸ (f)` cut out
by the `(|ι| - 1)`-st Fitting ideal of its differentials (the singular locus, in the smooth setting
of the module docstring) is unramified over `K` and contains the closed point, then `f ∈ 𝔪²` and
the Hessian determinant of `f` is a unit. This is the local case of
`Module.Basis.forall_mem_and_det_hessian_notMem_of_formallyUnramified`. -/
theorem mem_maximalIdeal_sq_and_isUnit_det_hessian_of_formallyUnramified [CommRing K]
    [Algebra K P] [Module.Finite (P ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) Ω[(P ⧸ Ideal.span {f})⁄K]]
    (b : Module.Basis ι P Ω[P⁄K]) (hx : maximalIdeal P = Ideal.span (Set.range x))
    (hb : ∀ i, b i = D K P (x i))
    [Algebra.FormallyUnramified K ((P ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) ⧸
      fittingIdeal (P ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) Ω[(P ⧸ Ideal.span {f})⁄K] (Fintype.card ι - 1))]
    (hsing : fittingIdeal (P ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) Ω[(P ⧸ Ideal.span {f})⁄K] (Fintype.card ι - 1) ≠
      ⊤) :
    f ∈ maximalIdeal P ^ 2 ∧ IsUnit (hessian (fun i ↦ (b.coord i).compDer (D K P)) f).det := by
  have hle : (fittingIdeal (P ⧸ Ideal.span {f}) Ω[(P ⧸ Ideal.span {f})⁄K]
      (Fintype.card ι - 1)).comap (Ideal.Quotient.mk _) ≤ maximalIdeal P :=
    le_maximalIdeal fun h ↦ hsing (Ideal.comap_eq_top_iff.1 h)
  have hf : f ∈ maximalIdeal P := hle <| by
    rw [Ideal.mem_comap, Ideal.Quotient.eq_zero_iff_mem.2 (Ideal.mem_span_singleton_self f)]
    exact zero_mem _
  have hD (i j : ι) : (b.coord i).compDer (D K P) (x j) = if i = j then 1 else 0 := by
    simp [← hb, Finsupp.single_apply, eq_comm]
  obtain ⟨hcrit, hdet⟩ := b.forall_mem_and_det_hessian_notMem_of_formallyUnramified f _ hle
  exact ⟨(mem_maximalIdeal_sq_iff_forall_apply_mem hx hD hf).2 hcrit,
    notMem_maximalIdeal.1 hdet⟩

end TauCeti
